  "chitchat": [
    "Bishop stands at the foot of the VIP stair with his hands folded, moving only his eyes.",
    "\"Rope's not personal. Rope's just math.\"",
    "He unclips the velvet rope for someone with a band, clips it again before you can follow."
  ],
  "description": "Bishop holds the foot of the VIP stair the way a load-bearing wall holds a roof: without apparent effort and without moving. Immaculate black, an earpiece, a hand-scanner clipped at his hip, and a stillness that reads every approach before it arrives. He is unfailingly polite, which somehow makes the rope harder to argue with. Buy a band and the stair opens like it was always going to. Try it without one and discover how far his patience does not extend.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "band": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "I'll take a band.",
          "next": "__shop__"
        },
        {
          "label": "Maybe later.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Band's the whole conversation. You get one from me, the reader on the stair reads it, the rope stops being my problem and starts being your good time.\" A small, professional smile. \"It is not cheap. That is the entire point of it.\""
    },
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "\"Enjoy your night.\" His gaze has already moved past you to the door."
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "What's upstairs?",
          "next": "upstairs"
        },
        {
          "label": "I want a VIP band.",
          "next": "band"
        },
        {
          "label": "Just heading in.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Evening.\" Bishop's eyes finish reading you before he speaks. \"Floor's open to everyone: drink, dance, be good. Stair's a different tier.\" A beat. \"You look like you're about to ask about the stair.\""
    },
    "upstairs": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "How do I get up there?",
          "next": "band"
        },
        {
          "label": "Forget it.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "He doesn't look at the stair. He doesn't have to. \"Up there is quiet, and the quiet costs. Booths, bottle service, a pour called Arc Light that the floor bar will deny exists.\" He shrugs, one centimetre. \"Get a band and it's all yours.\""
    }
  },
